A loop at the top of a body renders between the siblings written around it.

On fyne and gtk4 a reactive slot at the top of a window body, or of a
component body built at run time, renders into a `__root` container, and that
container is what the body renders as. So its static siblings have to be in it
too, in the order they were written: each is added ahead of the slot render
that follows it, which is what puts the slot's anchor after them, and the rest
are added once the body ends.

Before, fyne's window collected the static siblings into `parts` after the body
and assigned them to `__root.Objects`, discarding what the slots had rendered
there -- the rows were never shown, and a window with one static sibling
returned that sibling and left `__root` unparented. gtk4 appended the siblings
after the slots had rendered, so every row sat above the header. A component
instance put its whole `__root` at the first slot's position, so a static
sibling written between two loops rendered after both.

Only the render calls written at the top of the body are positions. `Card`'s
`flip` handler re-renders a slot into the same `__root`, and is not one.

The executed half is `TestRootSlotsKeepTheirPlaceRuns` in both platforms,
which reads the rendered order off the built tree and pushes to the list.

deny out/go/fyne/model.go `__root\.Objects = parts` -- assigning the static siblings over __root drops what the slots rendered into it
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `container\.NewVBox\([^)]*c\.__root` -- an instance's __root is its widget, not one sibling placed at its first slot
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `BoxAppend\(__box, c\.__root\)` -- likewise on gtk4
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `(?m)^\t\tc\.__root\.Add\(` -- a handler re-rendering a slot is not a position in the body, so nothing is added to __root inside one
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `(?m)^\t\tgtk4rt\.BoxAppend\(c\.__root` -- likewise on gtk4

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}

component Row(label string) ui.node {
    var n = 0
    ui.button(text="{label} {n}", @click { n += 1 })
}

component Card(xs list[string]) ui.node {
    var open = true
    ui.text(value="[")
    for var x = xs {
        ui.text(value=x)
    }
    ui.text(value="|")
    if open {
        ui.text(value="open")
    }
    ui.text(value="]")
    ui.button(text="flip", @click { open = !open })
}

ui.window {
    var items = ["a", "b"]
    ui.text(value="header")
    for var it = items {
        Row(label=it)
    }
    ui.text(value="mid")
    for var it = items {
        Card(xs=[it])
    }
    ui.text(value="footer")
    ui.button #more(text="more", @click { items.push("c") })
}
